# swarm-comms.suite — apps and nodes of one swarm reach each other on the first
# attempt, and stay reachable when the swarm changes and when a node is
# expelled: flows F1-F4 and the local edge cases M1-M6, M8 and M11-M14 of the
# E2E tests exhibit (https://wiki.satforge.dev/doc/e2e-tests-X3LHjItA2b), and
# the existing tests each flow rests on.
#
# Companion: swarm-comms-netsim.suite holds F5, the VM form of F6, M7, M9, M10
# and tor-link, nat-punch, gateway-relay and nearby-* (operator decision D11,
# 2026-11-20). This suite needs no netsim: every world is local. The
# companion needs netsim.
#
# Green (D11): 5 consecutive script runs and 1 agent run at a named astrald
# commit; the companion 3 runs or a recorded waiver.
#
# Agent forms: no F or M flow here ships a prompt.md. Five existing tests do:
# bootstrap-user-software-key, adopt-node, swarm-roster-sync, expel-node and
# expel-propagation (the last two are tests F4 rests on). `--driver agent`
# drives each of those named alone, e.g.
# `./tests/run --driver agent --docker expel-node`, and refuses the whole
# suite (app-call-remote ships no prompt.md). The flows have no agent form
# because the operator sits on node1 alone, and a node answers
# apphost.register and apphost.register_handler to a local caller only
# (astral-docs protocols/apphost/ops/), so no operator hosts an app on
# another node:
# - F1 swarm-apps-talk, F2 swarm-everyone-reaches-everyone, F4
#   swarm-expel-clean, M1 relay-contract-race and M11 expel-cross-traffic
#   judge the records of apps on every sibling;
# - the F3 chain's oracles judge the f3 mesh apps' records on the test host,
#   the harness performs its restarts, stop and freeze, and
#   swarm-survives-churn is local_only, a world no operator runs in.
# The "1 agent run" of Green has to be met by those five tests or waived; no
# flow of this suite can supply it.
#
# The order is a preference among siblings; the planner computes the run order
# from each test's `after`. `./tests/run --plan swarm-comms.suite` shows it.

